# middleware/ is not ours, and `Files: *` above must not be read as claiming it: the
# binary this package conveys links it static, and each library keeps its own copyright
# and licence (zlib, MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, and stb's public-domain alternative).
# The record is generated at utils/doc/THIRD-PARTY.md from the pins the repo keeps
# (gitlinks, bootstrap.sh's GLEW pin, the vendored headers' version macros) and installed
# next to this file as THIRD-PARTY.md; it says which library, which version, which
# licence. Each library's own notice text goes under
# /usr/share/doc/openspaceprogram/third-party/.
# The "License:" line below is deliberately a pointer rather than a licence name: naming
# one licence here would be a guess about fourteen different texts.
Files: middleware/*
Copyright: each library's own upstream -- see /usr/share/doc/openspaceprogram/THIRD-PARTY.md
License: see /usr/share/doc/openspaceprogram/THIRD-PARTY.md

